              "message": {
                "text": "root_control"
              },
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/vault.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 473,
                  "startLine": 450
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Sompi package version 0.8.0 at revision `4ebb82d4f82bac46ae3addd112c4752f29630a8a` can treat a provisional vault deposit reported by one Kaspa RPC as a completed Treasury Movement. The vault observer performs strong equality checks on the locally signed transaction, output index, amount, covenant identity, and script. It nevertheless accepts the matching output at `blockDaaScore=0` and carries that value into an `observedAtDaa` field that no later component enforces. The direct-Treasury adapter then writes the prepared covenant and current outpoint into `vault/config.json`, and the Treasury operation becomes terminal. If the reported output subsequently disappears\u2014or never existed in canonical history\u2014the process continues to load the nonexistent outpoint after restart. Automated use of the configured vault is then unavailable until the operator reconstructs or repairs its state."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "codexSecurity/v1": "codex-security/v1:sha256:eb6c5d253f47c4eff68fe2f1096d73c270ad52c7815726245aa8f1b97b2e7775"
          },
